    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0401" n="387" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p1/pg387"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/9–1448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in India
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-14T12:00:00-04:00">September 14,
                            1948—12 noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>552. Ref Deptel 551, you should bear in mind
                    that if Hyderabad situation comes to SC or if
                    Pakistani-Indian relations already before Council deteriorate significantly
                    because of Hyderabad, US must be free to pursue policy in SC in support of maintenance of international <pb facs="0402"
                        n="388" xml:id="pg388"/> peace and against use of force for settlement of
                    differences. In discussing Deptel 551 with
                        GOI, therefore, you should not in any way
                    imply that we condone use of force respecting Hyderabad.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
